{"title":"Gap lemma","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Gap lemma</b> is actually a trivial corollary of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Least_upper_bound\" title=\"Least upper bound\">completeness property</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> but is extremely useful in real analysis\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gap_lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc367d27a247f0657c3dc353e448f804cdeaf29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\subset\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> be bounded above\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4adfbc7511383e6a20b82357f349ac6f851e978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=\\sup{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1ccca5cf199647ac8792afd47d075779fbb02f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall\\epsilon&gt;0\\;\\;\\exists a\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df00f7fa004ef70e27a0a9f5b25db2d76de76776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|u-a|&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gap_lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume if possible, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecf8666cca5f1d089b9c656be83f9e09d0abd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists$\" width=\"9\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6da49fefb1906c55ed166a63282b0d8e19ca31c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a852b35254955f79b530ce822523217d2da7bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|u-a|&gt;\\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536ba5a392431e74fec5a8db2257504c85fcc206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a50f85686fe7cb27b1ae676014e18fc9e46e9bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/1511b8ad072686eeb223d27d6a7025c3e5149c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u&#39;=u-\\delta$\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf5efcef43c2817703d4c1980182a480889e12f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u&#39;$\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is an upper bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de458e1f54a8046903771af4f0f72573eb65c0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u&#39;&lt;u$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> which contradicts the assumption that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4adfbc7511383e6a20b82357f349ac6f851e978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=\\sup{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Gap_lemma&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085329\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 68/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2618/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.024      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.024      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6422:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018085329 and revision id 23282. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}